# Arigami behind Caddy — LAN / no public DNS: self-signed via Caddy's internal CA.
#
# Answers ANY name on :443 (arigami.lan, the machine's mDNS name, its LAN IP…)
# with a certificate minted on the fly by the internal CA — no env needed.
#   ARIGAMI_UPSTREAM / ARIGAMI_RATELIMIT_FILE as in Caddyfile.
#
# Clients must trust Caddy's root CA once (docs/TLS.md → "LAN"): on the Caddy
# machine `caddy trust`, elsewhere install
# <caddy data dir>/pki/authorities/local/root.crt. For phones prefer
# `tailscale serve` (real certificate, nothing to install).
#
# The host must be told the same origin: ARIGAMI_PUBLIC_URL=https://<name>
# — or leave it unset and rely on trustProxy + X-Forwarded-Proto (loopback only).

import arigami.caddy

https://:443 {
	tls internal
	import arigami
}
